From 94d8d892e37e225b13198156f33082242a0e490d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 20:46:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] player information: the Dolby Vision page says only what the
 overview does not

The two Dolby Vision pages (5555, and "Dolby Vision: pictures", 5557)
repeated most of the overview page (5556): the output and why, the
profile, the layers and FEL, L1, L2, L5, L6, the frames shown and the
gaps, the GPU time and headroom, the path, the frame ahead and the
step-down, the mode. Each is now in one place, the overview. One Dolby
Vision page is left, with what only it says: the output chosen for this
video (its button), the transport, what the link carries for native
output and the older HDMI 1.4b signalling where it is used, what the
display offers for Dolby Vision, that Kodi's scaling method is not used
by the Dolby Vision engine, and the passes that took the most GPU time
(dvpasstimes). Its tab is shown only where one of those rows can be (no
empty panel), and also for an HDR10 or HDR10+ video whose output can be
chosen.

make-playerinfo.py takes the one page; system/hades made again. Test
(host): every row of the two old pages is on the new page or what it
reads is on the overview (21 rows), the tab covers every row, and the
page for every skin is that of Estuary; make-playerinfo.py --check and
pi_check2.py pass. Not seen on a screen.
